.TH smi-restorecon "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-restorecon \- Restore the SELinux file contexts of a directory tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-restorecon
.I DIRECTORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-restorecon
runs
.B restorecon -Rv
on
.IR DIRECTORY ,
resetting the SELinux file contexts of the whole tree to what the policy says they should be and
printing every change.
It is what a directory needs after files have been copied or unpacked into it from somewhere
else, for example a web root filled from a deployment archive, which otherwise keeps the context
of where it came from and is then refused by the service that should read it.
.PP
Changing the contexts of files of other users needs root.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
Directory tree to relabel.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
The exit status of
.BR restorecon (8).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
After unpacking a site into the nginx web root:
.RS
.nf
smi-xvzf site.tar.gz /usr/share/nginx/html ALL_IN_ROOT=true
sudo smi-restorecon /usr/share/nginx/html
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
